osfmk/kern/kpc.h and the arm64 KPC sources use CORE_NCTRS to size their
counter arrays whether or not the target enables performance counters, and
the BCM2837 board config never defines it. The result is 62 "use of
undeclared identifier 'CORE_NCTRS'" errors across kpc.h, kperf_kpc.h,
kpc_common.c, kpc.c and monotonic.h.

Give the target the same placeholder the later Apple configs use. Nothing
reads these counters on this board; the value only has to be a sane bound.

--- a/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/board_config.h
+++ b/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/board_config.h
@@ -172,6 +172,9 @@
 #define __ARM_L2CACHE_SIZE_LOG__ 19
 #define ARM_BOARD_CLASS_BCM2837
 #define CPU_COUNT 4
+/* KPC is not enabled for this target, but osfmk/kern/kpc.h and the
+ * arm64 KPC sources size their arrays with CORE_NCTRS regardless. */
+#define CORE_NCTRS 8
 #endif  /* ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_BCM2837 */
 
 #endif /* ! _PEXPERT_ARM_BOARD_CONFIG_H */
